---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { story } from "../content/images";
---

<section class="story" aria-labelledby="story-title-1">
  <div class="story__row">
    <div class="story__text reveal">
      <h2 class="story__title" id="story-title-1">Make that process<br />feel much simpler</h2>
      <p data-words>
          Walking somewhere new usually starts the same way: open a map, search for places, save a few pins, check the distance, then try to turn all of that into a route.
      </p>
      <p data-words>
          Walk&amp;Sight started with one idea: choose how much time you have, how far you want to walk and what interests you. The app does the rest by building a walking route around places worth discovering.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="story__media reveal">
      <Image src={story.one} alt="A couple looking around a sunlit square, one holding a phone and the other a paper map" widths={[640, 960, 1280]} sizes="(min-width: 1920px) 880px, (min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" quality={80} format="webp" />
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="story__row story__row--flip">
    <div class="story__text reveal">
      <h2 class="story__title">Walk&amp;Sight was designed to make discovery feel lightweight</h2>
      <p data-words>Walk&amp;Sight was designed to make discovery feel lightweight.</p>
      <p data-words>
          The interface helps you make a few decisions, understand the route and start moving without turning the experience into another complex map application.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="story__media reveal">
      <Image src={story.two} alt="A smiling couple checking a route on a phone together" widths={[640, 960, 1280]} sizes="(min-width: 1920px) 880px, (min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" quality={80} format="webp" />
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
